## Highlights
- Study of simple transmembrane proteins reveals principles of protein interactions- Most simple transmembrane proteins are biologically active in mammalian cells- Ultra-simple transmembrane proteins use diverse mechanisms of action- Effects of multiple mutations in these simple proteins are not additive- Specific rules that establish transmembrane interactions remain elusive
